This is the vendor repository package for KSA Technologies plugins.
Install it once, then the plugins it provides appear under
System > Firmware > Plugins and update with normal firmware updates.

It adds two package repositories:

* KSA:       released plugins (os-sbc), one track per major version
* KSA-devel: development builds from the plugins' next branch, off by
             default; create /usr/local/etc/pkg/KSA-devel.enable and
             reinstall this package to opt in

Both are signed; the fingerprint is installed with this package.
Plugins provided: os-sbc, a SIP Session Border Controller
(Kamailio and rtpproxy), with its Kamailio and rtpproxy packages.
